<article class="env-lemma" id="0EIU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EIU">Lemma <span data-tag="0EIU">52.17.1</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EHC" data-tag="0EHC">52.16.1</a>. Let $(\mathcal{F}_ n) \to (\mathcal{F}'_ n)$ be a morphism of $\textit{Coh}(U, I\mathcal{O}_ U)$ whose kernel and cokernel are annihilated by a power of $I$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$(\mathcal{F}_ n)$ extends to $X$ if and only if $(\mathcal{F}'_ n)$ extends to $X$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$(\mathcal{F}_ n)$ is the completion of a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ U$-module if and only if $(\mathcal{F}'_ n)$ is. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (2) follows immediately from Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0889" data-tag="0889">30.23.6</a>. To see part (1), we first use Lemma <a href="/tag/0EIN" data-tag="0EIN">52.16.6</a> to reduce to the case where $A$ is $I$-adically complete. However, in that case (1) reduces to (2) by Lemma <a href="/tag/0EIL" data-tag="0EIL">52.16.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>